diff --git a/docs/development.md b/docs/development.md
index 0bca076..df586c8 100644
--- a/docs/development.md
+++ b/docs/development.md
@@ -72,6 +72,17 @@ bin/rails dev:email
 
 Under the hood, this will create or remove `tmp/email-dev.txt`.
 
+### Languages
+
+Fizzy speaks English and Japanese. Opening any page with `?locale=ja` (or `?locale=en`) switches the language for
+the rest of the browser session and remembers the choice on the identity, so it follows people to their next sign-in.
+Unknown locales are ignored. People who never chose anything keep getting English.
+
+Translations live in `config/locales/<locale>/*.yml`, split by area, and views use lazy lookups (`t(".key")`).
+Everything rendered for a specific person outside of a request — emails, push notifications, Turbo broadcasts — runs
+inside `identity.in_locale` / `user.in_locale`. `test/i18n_test.rb` fails when the locales fall out of sync, so add
+every new key to both languages.
+
 ## SaaS gem
 
 37signals bundles Fizzy with [`fizzy-saas`](https://github.com/basecamp/fizzy/tree/main/saas), a companion gem that links Fizzy with our billing system and contains our production setup.
